From 89ea653e98e009c4284a961bfeef879f95cb7d9b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: abhay-byte <abhay02delhi@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 16:50:50 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jm-v7 050: bindless update-after-bind and mutable bindings on
 v6/v7

Bifrost copies descriptors per draw into per-type hardware tables (16-bit
texture/sampler counts, 256 storage images). That cannot cover
update-after-bind arrays of a million descriptors nor mutable bindings, so
such bindings (panvk_binding_is_bindless()) are read from the set memory:

- Storage images and storage/uniform texel buffers: the shader decodes the
  set descriptor (ATTRIBUTE_BUFFER + CONTINUATION_3D / ATTRIBUTE), computes
  the texel address (linear or 16x16 u-interleaved), and uses LD_CVT/ST_CVT
  with an INTERNAL_CONVERSION built from the view format and the access
  type, or global atomics. Out-of-bounds loads read the zeroed page through
  the view format (robustImageAccess2 values), stores/atomics are skipped.
- Textures and samplers: a shader touching a bindless texture (sampler)
  binding switches its whole texture (sampler) table to direct indexing:
  the DCD table points at a device-constant base 64 GiB below the device
  dummy sampler, and the index is desc.direct_idx[set] + descriptor index
  (new sysvals). RSD texture/sampler count is 0xFFFF. Samplerless ops in a
  direct-sampler shader use the device dummy sampler (desc.dummy_sampler_idx).
- Mutable SSBOs use the SSBO address format; v6/v7 mutable lists exclude
  UBOs. The jm-v7 048 robust image pass skips bindless images.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
